                        "review": "Look, Crush Crush is cute, I won't fault it that. There are a lot of girls, a lot of good art, some good stories, some good voice acting, and some genuinely funny humor. The fact it's free to play is the chef's kiss on top.\r\n\r\nAt the same time, none of that justifies just how unfun this game is. Without spending money on Gems and the DLC girls, the game is very slow and very repetitive, letting it idle for days just to unlock the stats or in game cash to level up a girl once and get 1-to-3 more precious Gems and a few more lines of dialogue, maybe one picture. And while every idle/clicker game has timers and prestige and slogs, Crush Crush just doesn't offer up enough reward or variety without opening your wallet repeatedly. You practically NEED to Gem enhance every skill and multiple jobs on top of the prestige multiplier to get things working for some of the girls to progress, and the cost of 200 Gems and/or dozens of real life dollars to unlock some of the girls is just egregious. You shouldn't be able to spend hundreds of dollars on a kind of silly/vapid idle dating sim game, let alone feel like you have to in order to get the most out of it and have fun. \r\n\r\nI really wish I could be more positive looking back on all the time I spent with Crush Crush. There's clearly a lot of love put into it with the humor and writing and voice acting. And there really is a good variety to the girls once you start unlocking them. It just all takes way too long and is too boring. It feels more like a job than a game, more so even then other mobile style games with login bonuses and idle elements. Still, I can't speak for everyone on the game, and there is a possibility you'll have a different experience then me; Maybe you feel less pressure to log in every day religiously to do the events and check up on your progress. Maybe you don't mind spending the money for the girls so much. Maybe you are simply more patient and content and are fine simply letting the game idle for days on end and unlocking whatever unlocks, with no pressure for the game to move at any particular pace or offer up new content. And I wouldn't fault you for that; Like I said, it really is a cute game and it's hard to beat free. \r\n\r\nIt's just not for me; I already have enough work and daily routines and things to wait for in my life. I don't need a game on my computer feeling like yet another obligation.",
